  "created": "2022-11-09T04:00:40.141Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently, debug information used to show current animator states in the in-game AV3 debug menu is captured as part of VRCSdkControlPanelAvatarBuilder3A.ValidateFeatures(), which is invoked prior to running avatar preprocessing hooks. As a result, if any avatar preprocessing hooks manipulate AV3 animator controller, these states show up as [UNKNOWN] in the in-game debug menu.\nThis debug state computation should be done after all preprocessing hooks are completed instead. Or, alternately, an API should be provided to recompute these values (it's possible to invoke ValidateFeatures from an editor script/preprocess hook as a workaround, but it's kind of obvious that this is not a supported API today)",
